.TH ZERODDS-ROS2.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ros2.yaml \- the ros2 section of the ZeroDDS runtime configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/zerodds.yaml
.br
.I /etc/zerodds/zerodds.d/50-ros2.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I rmw_zerodds_cpp
reads its ROS settings from the runtime configuration every ZeroDDS program
reads: the base file
.IR zerodds.yaml ,
the drop-ins in
.I zerodds.d
in name order,
.I include:
files, and the environment beneath them. As every ZeroDDS program, the RMW
takes
.B \-\-config
.I FILE
(another base with
.IR FILE.d/ )
and
.B \-\-set
.I path=value
(above all files) from the command line, here the command line of the ROS
process outside its
.B \-\-ros\-args
\&... \-\- blocks, which belong to rcl.
The section is
.BR ros2 ;
a drop-in holding only that section is the usual form. There is no separate
shim file. The schema is
.IR zerodds-ros2-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I Ros2Config::from_config
in
.IR crates/rmw-zerodds-shim/src/ros2_config.rs .
.PP
The RMW checks the section when
.I rmw_init
runs: an unknown key or an invalid value fails initialisation, with the
setting, its file and line on stderr.
.B zerodds-ros2-shim \-\-check\-config
prints the same result before a node starts. Other programs reading the same
files leave the section to the RMW.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B topic_mangling
.IR rmw " (default): the " rt/
prefix of REP-2007;
.IR none :
the ROS name without its leading slash, for coexistence with DDS
applications;
.IR custom :
the prefix in
.B custom_mangling
.BR topic_prefix ,
which is then required and is refused otherwise. A service
.I /add_two_ints
has the DDS topics
.I rq/add_two_intsRequest
and
.IR rr/add_two_intsReply ,
as with the other RMWs; under
.I none
without the prefixes, under
.I custom
with
.B custom_mangling
.B request_prefix
and
.B response_prefix
(default
.IR rq/ ", " rr/ ).
An application's
.I avoid_ros_namespace_conventions
drops any prefix: the DDS topic is the ROS name with its leading slash, as
with the other RMWs.
.TP
.B qos_profiles
Map of named profiles. The built-in table is REP-2009:
.I sensor_data
KEEP_LAST(5) BEST_EFFORT VOLATILE,
.I services
KEEP_LAST(10) RELIABLE VOLATILE,
.I parameters
KEEP_LAST(1000) RELIABLE VOLATILE,
.I parameter_events
KEEP_ALL RELIABLE VOLATILE,
.I default
KEEP_LAST(10) RELIABLE VOLATILE. An entry, such as
.B sensor_data
in the example, replaces the fields it names; a new name adds a profile.
Fields:
.BR reliability " (" \fIreliable\fR " | " \fIbest_effort\fR " | " \fIsystem_default\fR ),
.BR durability " (" \fIvolatile\fR " | " \fItransient_local\fR " | " \fIsystem_default\fR ),
.BR history " (" \fIkeep_last\fR " | " \fIkeep_all\fR " | " \fIsystem_default\fR ),
.BR depth ,
.BR deadline_ms ,
.BR lifespan_ms ,
.BR liveliness " (" \fIautomatic\fR " | " \fImanual_by_topic\fR " | " \fIsystem_default\fR ),
.BR liveliness_lease_ms .
A duration of 0 means none.
.TP
.B topic_overrides
List of entries, each with
.B ros_topic
(the ROS name before mangling) and either
.B qos_profile
(a name of the table) or
.B qos
(a map of the fields above). The entry replaces those fields of what the
application requests on that topic;
.I rmw_*_get_actual_qos
reports the result.
.TP
.B time_based_filter
TIME_BASED_FILTER minimum_separation in seconds, for every topic
.RI ( 0.1 )
or per topic
.RI ( /scan=0.1 ),
a comma list; environment
.IR ZERODDS_TIME_BASED_FILTER .
.TP
.B spatial_bridge
C2(6) — an opt-in content-translation daemon (its own
.IR DomainParticipant ,
not part of the RMW's own runtime) that republishes
.I zerodds-spatial-dds
topics as the matching ROS 2
.I zerodds-spatial-ros2
type and back
.RI ( crates/rmw\-zerodds\-shim/src/spatial_bridge.rs ).
.B enabled
(default false)
starts it;
.B mappings
is a list of entries, each:
.BR message " (" \fIpose_stamped\fR ", " \fItransform_stamped\fR ", " \fIgeo_pose_stamped\fR ", " \fIdetection3d\fR ", " \fIdetection3d_array\fR " or " \fIimu\fR "; "
.I tf_message
is refused by name — no reverse conversion exists for it, and its forward
one bundles several samples, not one at a time),
.BR spatial_topic " (the " zerodds\-spatial\-dds
DCPS topic name, e.g.
.IR sdds/default/FramedPose ),
.BR ros_topic " (the ROS logical name, e.g. " /robot1/pose ,
mangled the same way every other ROS topic on this RMW is), and
.BR direction " (" \fIdds_to_ros\fR ", " \fIros_to_dds\fR " or " \fIboth\fR ",
default
.IR both ).
Every SpatialDDS-only field a conversion drops (or defaults, going back) is
named in
.IR zerodds\-spatial\-ros2 's
own field-fidelity doc comment and reported once per
.RI ( topic ", " direction )
as an observability event
.RI ( diagnostics.observability ,
name
.IR spatial_bridge.field_fidelity ),
never silently. The SpatialDDS side's DDS type name follows the fixed
convention
.I spatial::<module>::<Type>
(mirroring the Rust module path in
.IR zerodds\-spatial\-dds );
a SpatialDDS publisher/subscriber this bridge talks to must use the same
string — DDS matches by topic name
.I and
type name, and this is not XTypes-hash-checked.
.SS refused
Each is refused with where the value belongs:
.I ros2.namespace
(rcl resolves names with the node namespace:
.IR "\-\-ros\-args \-r __ns:=/ns" ),
.I ros2.ros_domain_id
.RI ( ROS_DOMAIN_ID ),
.I ros2.enclave
.RI ( security.enclave_dir ),
.I logging
(rcutils:
.IR "\-\-ros\-args \-\-log\-level" ),
.I discovery.multicast
and
.I discovery.unicast_initial_peers
.RI ( discovery.no_multicast ", " discovery.peers ).
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/ros2.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ros2-shim (1).
